  "label": "Information Control",
  "description": "Information control refers to the practice of restricting, manipulating, or shaping the flow of information to influence public opinion or behavior. The meme accuses Google of exerting control over what people see and hear, which is a real-world concern about the power of large tech companies over media and news. This concept is often discussed in political science, media studies, and digital rights discourse.",
